WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.678
Lisa and Frank stood outside Grandpa’s house.

2
00:00:03.679 --> 00:00:07.629
"Mom, I want to bring my sketch pad and crayons.

3
00:00:07.630 --> 00:00:11.915
I’m going to draw a picture of the lake," said Lisa.

4
00:00:11.916 --> 00:00:16.183
"I’m bringing my baseball and glove," said Frank.

5
00:00:16.184 --> 00:00:21.470
"Grandpa said he’s going to show me how to throw a curve ball."

6
00:00:21.471 --> 00:00:23.414
"Okay, but hurry.

7
00:00:23.415 --> 00:00:26.609
Dad is waiting," said Mom.

8
00:00:26.610 --> 00:00:29.237
Dad was waiting at the lake with the boat.

9
00:00:29.238 --> 00:00:34.938
"Daddy! Daddy! I became a big girl today!" shouted Lisa.

10
00:00:34.939 --> 00:00:39.138
"A big girl? Really?" asked Dad.

11
00:00:39.139 --> 00:00:43.874
"Yes, I’ve got a loose tooth. See?"

12
00:00:43.875 --> 00:00:49.542
"Wow!" exclaimed Dad. "You are a big girl."

13
00:00:49.543 --> 00:00:55.630
"See, see? Daddy, my tooth is out!" shouted Lisa excitedly.

14
00:00:55.631 --> 00:00:58.204
She held up her tooth.

15
00:00:58.205 --> 00:01:02.168
"What are you going to do with the tooth?" asked Dad.

16
00:01:02.169 --> 00:01:09.620
"Tonight I am going to put it under my pillow and make a wish," replied Lisa.

17
00:01:09.621 --> 00:01:12.787
"Oh, I see," said Dad.

18
00:01:12.788 --> 00:01:16.006
"What are you going to wish for?"

19
00:01:16.007 --> 00:01:20.105
"I don’t know yet," said Lisa, frowning.

20
00:01:20.106 --> 00:01:22.512
"I hadn’t thought about it."

21
00:01:22.513 --> 00:01:25.668
Grandpa arrived with the life jackets.

22
00:01:25.669 --> 00:01:30.476
"When you do know," warned Grandpa, "you mustn’t tell anyone.

23
00:01:30.477 --> 00:01:34.405
The tooth fairy only grants secret wishes."

24
00:01:34.406 --> 00:01:37.916
"Oh! Daddy, I can’t tell you my wish.

25
00:01:37.917 --> 00:01:42.417
It’s a secret," said Lisa seriously.

26
00:01:42.418 --> 00:01:46.094
"Are we going in the boat?" asked Frank.

27
00:01:46.095 --> 00:01:48.741
"Yes," said Dad.

28
00:01:48.742 --> 00:01:52.728
"We are going to take the boat to the island."

29
00:01:52.729 --> 00:01:54.125
"To the island?

30
00:01:54.126 --> 00:01:58.744
Are there pirates on the island?" asked Lisa.

31
00:01:58.745 --> 00:02:01.623
"No," said Grandpa.

32
00:02:01.624 --> 00:02:07.585
"But a beautiful Native American princess once lived on the island."

33
00:02:07.586 --> 00:02:13.043
"Really?" asked Lisa. "What was her name?"

34
00:02:13.044 --> 00:02:15.050
"Her name was Sunapee.

35
00:02:15.051 --> 00:02:20.146
The lake and the island are both named after her," answered Grandpa.

36
00:02:20.147 --> 00:02:24.522
"Why did she live on the island?" asked Frank.

37
00:02:24.523 --> 00:02:33.271
"She lived on the island because the man she loved died, and she didn’t want to marry any other man," said Grandpa.

38
00:02:33.272 --> 00:02:39.101
"Oh," said Lisa. "It must have been very lonely."

39
00:02:39.102 --> 00:02:43.399
"No, not lonely at all," answered Grandpa.

40
00:02:43.400 --> 00:02:49.690
"She was loved by all of the animals, especially the eagle king."

41
00:02:49.691 --> 00:02:54.524
"What happened to the princess?" asked Frank.

42
00:02:54.525 --> 00:02:58.437
"No one knows for sure," answered Grandpa.

43
00:02:58.438 --> 00:03:03.241
When everyone was in the boat, Grandpa told the story.

44
00:03:03.242 --> 00:03:06.504
"The eagle king loved the princess very much.

45
00:03:06.505 --> 00:03:09.047
He protected her from all men.

46
00:03:09.048 --> 00:03:16.787
Many men tried to go to the island to marry the princess, but the eagle king fought each of them.

47
00:03:16.788 --> 00:03:24.186
"The Native Americans believe the princess married the eagle king because he was like her lost love."

48
00:03:24.187 --> 00:03:28.564
"Are there eagles on the island now?" asked Lisa.

49
00:03:28.565 --> 00:03:31.720
"Yes, many," answered Grandpa.

50
00:03:31.721 --> 00:03:36.090
"Will we see an eagle?" asked Frank.

51
00:03:36.091 --> 00:03:40.462
"Yes, you will see eagles," said Grandpa.

52
00:03:40.463 --> 00:03:44.799
Lisa and Frank both wanted to see the eagles.

53
00:03:44.800 --> 00:03:49.971
Lisa was so excited that she forgot about the tooth she was holding.

54
00:03:49.972 --> 00:03:54.824
"Oh no!" cried Lisa. "My tooth is gone.

55
00:03:54.825 --> 00:03:57.910
I dropped it, and it fell into the lake.

56
00:03:57.911 --> 00:04:03.248
Now I have nothing to give to the tooth fairy."

57
00:04:03.249 --> 00:04:06.757
"There will be other teeth," said Grandpa.

58
00:04:06.758 --> 00:04:14.034
"Yes, but I had finally decided what I was going to wish for," whined Lisa.

59
00:04:14.035 --> 00:04:24.760
"As long as you don’t tell anyone your wish, the tooth fairy will grant it to you next time," said Grandma.

60
00:04:24.761 --> 00:04:30.985
"Look!" shouted Frank. "Is that an eagle?"

61
00:04:30.986 --> 00:04:32.715
"It’s so high,"

62
00:04:32.716 --> 00:04:36.539
said Lisa, forgetting about her lost tooth.

63
00:04:36.540 --> 00:04:39.943
"Watch it closely," said Grandpa.

64
00:04:39.944 --> 00:04:43.641
The eagle flew close by, flapping its wings.

65
00:04:43.642 --> 00:04:48.186
"Wow!" shouted everyone.

66
00:04:48.187 --> 00:04:52.911
"Eagles are so fast!" exclaimed Frank.

67
00:04:52.912 --> 00:04:58.783
"A feather!" shouted Lisa. "I caught a feather!"

68
00:04:58.784 --> 00:05:04.062
"Grandpa," asked Lisa, "do eagle feathers grow back?"

69
00:05:04.063 --> 00:05:08.360
"Yes. Yes, they do," said Grandpa slowly.

70
00:05:08.361 --> 00:05:12.312
"They grow back—just like baby teeth."

71
00:05:12.313 --> 00:05:19.808
"Do you think I can put this feather under my pillow and make a wish?" asked Lisa.

72
00:05:19.809 --> 00:05:22.966
"Hmm," said Grandpa.

73
00:05:22.967 --> 00:05:26.742
"That’s an excellent question, but I don’t know the answer.

74
00:05:26.743 --> 00:05:29.276
I don’t know if there’s a feather fairy.

75
00:05:29.277 --> 00:05:33.446
I’ve never tried making a wish on a feather."

76
00:05:33.447 --> 00:05:37.607
"Well, I’m going to make a wish on my eagle feather.

77
00:05:37.608 --> 00:05:42.770
Maybe Princess Sunapee will grant me my wish!" said Lisa.

78
00:05:42.771 --> 00:05:46.532
"Maybe she will," smiled Grandpa.

79
00:05:46.533 --> 00:05:53.049
"If there is a tooth fairy," said Lisa, "then there has to be a feather fairy.

80
00:05:53.050 --> 00:05:59.383
I’m sure that my wish will come true."

